    "body": "<del>\r\nIn section of \"4.4.10 The menuitem element\";\r\nThe following sentence shoud be added as firest sentence of prose.\r\n```\r\nThe menuitem element represents command that the user can invoke, or a sub-menu that the user can trigger.\r\nThe menuitem element constitute contents of a menubar element or a menulist element.\r\n```\r\n</del>\r\n\r\nIn section of \"4.4.2 The hr element\";\r\n```\r\nThe hr element represents a paragraph-level thematic break, e.g., a scene change in a story, or a transition to another topic within a section of a reference book; alternatively, it represents a separator between a set of options of a select element.\r\n```\r\n　　↓should change\r\n```\r\nThe hr element represents a paragraph-level thematic break, e.g., a scene change in a story, or a transition to another topic within a section of a reference book; alternatively, it represents a separator between a set of options of a select element; alternatively, it represents a separator between a set of menuitem elements in a menulist element.\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nIn section of \"4.10.15 The fieldset element\";\r\n```\r\nThe fieldset element represents a set of form controls (or other content) grouped together, optionally with a caption. The caption is given by the first legend element that is a child of the fieldset element, if any. The remainder of the descendants form the group.\r\n```\r\n　　↓should change\r\n```\r\nThe fieldset element represents a set of form controls (or other content) grouped together, optionally with a caption. The caption is given by the first legend element that is a child of the fieldset element, if any. The remainder of the descendants form the group.\r\nAlternatively, it represents a set of menuitem elements in a menulist element.The label is given by the first legend element that is a child of the fieldset element, if any. \r\n```\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
