    "created_at": "2026-08-27T15:56:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-27T15:56:53Z",
    "body": "(I'll continue looking into this some more, but some generic feedback already)\r\n\r\nOverall the new approach seems a lot easier to understand and event handling works in a more natural way etc.\r\n\r\nI'm still not a big fan of fieldset and checkability handling. Makes it rather awkward to create menus like\r\n<img width=\"303\" height=\"227\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/88d78fc2-7e12-490f-bc72-2e008c25541f\" />\r\nand often the fieldset in menus seems to be just useless. submenu itself does quite a bit grouping, underneath that name attribute might work fine, if needed (usually it wouldn't be needed).",
